import{H as e,at as t,it as n,vt as r}from"./chunks/framework.dmHZ7NHG.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"The tides","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"params":{"slug":"tides","address":"2abbee78-81ce-8747-8253-bc8b75aa1c54","receipt":"07e85458-dce6-8af5-9c22-d66476368b6d"},"relativePath":"docs/publications/tides.md","filePath":"docs/publications/[slug].md"}`),a={name:`docs/publications/tides.md`};function o(e,i,a,o,s,c){return r(),n(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="the-tides" tabindex="-1">The tides <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-tides" aria-label="Permalink to “The tides”">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>the sailor&#39;s tides as decidable arithmetic, joining the captain&#39;s domain — the rule of twelfths (1,2,3,3,2,1 = 12, a palindrome of flood and ebb), half-tide by the third hour (1+2+3 = 6 of 12), the middle hours running three times faster than the turns (3 &gt; 1), the semidiurnal period of two highs a lunar day apart (12h25m = 745 min, ×2 = 24h50m), and spring exceeding neap as the Moon&#39;s phase adds or cancels the Sun&#39;s pull — tidal arithmetic, NOT a harmonic tide-prediction model</p></blockquote><p>These 7 facts hold by decision. Each was proven in Lean 4 — no Mathlib, checked sorry-free — and every sentence below links the proof that seals it. This note claims nothing beyond what its theorems settle: not that the domain is complete, only that the prose says nothing the proofs do not. It was written by reading the sealed ledger; read the proofs, not the prose.</p><h2 id="the-facts-each-backed-by-its-proof" tabindex="-1">The facts, each backed by its proof <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-facts-each-backed-by-its-proof" aria-label="Permalink to “The facts, each backed by its proof”">​</a></h2><ul><li>The sailor&#39;s rule of twelfths: over six hours a tide rises 1,2,3,3,2,1 twelfths of its range — and 1+2+3+3+2+1 = 12, the whole range accounted for. — <a href="/theorem/rule_of_twelfths">proof</a>.</li><li>The rule is a palindrome — [1,2,3,3,2,1] reversed is itself: flood and ebb mirror, the tide fills as it drains. — <a href="/theorem/twelfths_symmetric">proof</a>.</li><li>By the third hour the water stands at HALF its range: 1+2+3 = 6 of 12 (2·6 = 12) — half-tide falls at mid-flood, not the halfway time by accident but by the twelfths. — <a href="/theorem/half_tide_at_hour_three">proof</a>.</li><li>The middle hours run fastest: 3 twelfths an hour at mid-tide versus 1 at the turns — 3 &gt; 1, so the water moves most where a grounded keel most needs the depth to change. — <a href="/theorem/mid_tide_fastest">proof</a>.</li><li>Two high tides fall a lunar day apart: 12h25m = 745 minutes each, and 745·2 = 1490 = 24h50m — the semidiurnal rhythm, set by the Moon, not the Sun (which would give 24h). — <a href="/theorem/semidiurnal_period">proof</a>.</li><li>A spring tide (new or full Moon, Sun and Moon aligned, their pulls ADD) exceeds a neap (at the quarter, pulls partly cancel): 2+1 &gt; 2−1 — the range swells and shrinks with the phase. — <a href="/theorem/spring_exceeds_neap">proof</a>.</li><li>One semidiurnal cycle is six hours of flood and six of ebb: 6 + 6 = 12 — the tide gives back exactly the hours it took. — <a href="/theorem/flood_and_ebb">proof</a>.</li></ul><h2 id="provenance" tabindex="-1">Provenance <a class="header-anchor" href="#provenance" aria-label="Permalink to “Provenance”">​</a></h2><p>These 7 proofs fold, order-invariant, to the receipt <code>07e85458-dce6-8af5-9c22-d66476368b6d</code> — recompute it from the same ledger and it returns. The note itself content-addresses to a uuid, so any edit is visible. Writing descends from reading: this note holds only what the proofs it links already sealed, and it was audited by uuidna&#39;s own honesty gate before it was published — a sentence that overreached a proof would have been refused, not shipped.</p><p>Source · <a href="https://github.com/uuidna/uuidna/blob/main/lean/Tides.lean" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">lean/Tides.lean</a> · <a href="/theorems">all theorems</a></p><hr><p><strong>Audited before published</strong> · this note passed uuidna&#39;s honesty gate at build time — every claim above links the proof that seals it. Content-address <code>2abbee78</code> · proofs fold to receipt <code>07e85458</code> (the handles; the full uuids are in this page&#39;s meta, recomputable) · 7 sealed theorems.</p><p><a href="/publications">All publications</a> · <a href="/theorems">All theorems</a> · <a href="/trials">How auditing works</a></p>`,11)]])}var s=e(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};